WEBVTT

00:00:14.421 --> 00:00:53.426
Jide presents The Happy Prince and The Selfish Giant by Oscar Wilde The Happy Prince Part 1 The Ruby On a tall column in the city, there is a statue of the Happy Prince.

00:00:53.486 --> 00:00:56.538
He is covered with gold.

00:00:56.598 --> 00:01:00.980
He has two blue sapphires for eyes.

00:01:01.040 --> 00:01:05.484
On his sword, there is a big red ruby.

00:01:05.544 --> 00:01:08.574
He is very beautiful.

00:01:08.634 --> 00:01:13.886
Everyone in the city likes the statue of the Happy Prince.

00:01:13.946 --> 00:01:17.439
Look at the Happy Prince!

00:01:17.499 --> 00:01:20.590
Says a mother to her little boy.

00:01:20.650 --> 00:01:22.932
He never cries.

00:01:22.992 --> 00:01:26.134
He is always happy.

00:01:26.194 --> 00:01:30.867
One night a little swallow flies over the city.

00:01:30.927 --> 00:01:36.032
His friends are in Egypt and he wants to go there too.

00:01:36.092 --> 00:01:40.035
He sees the statue on the tall column.

00:01:40.095 --> 00:01:41.006
Oh!

00:01:41.066 --> 00:01:43.858
What a beautiful statue!

00:01:43.918 --> 00:01:46.790
I have a golden bedroom.

00:01:46.849 --> 00:01:50.212
I can sleep here near the prince's feet.

00:01:50.272 --> 00:01:52.514
He says to himself.

00:01:52.574 --> 00:01:56.286
He puts his head under his wing.

00:01:56.346 --> 00:02:01.099
Suddenly a big drop of water falls on him.

00:02:01.159 --> 00:02:03.890
Then another drop falls.

00:02:03.950 --> 00:02:06.142
How strange!

00:02:06.202 --> 00:02:11.633
There aren't any clouds in the sky, but it's raining.

00:02:11.693 --> 00:02:16.535
Another drop falls and the swallow looks up.

00:02:16.595 --> 00:02:20.646
The happy prince is crying.

00:02:20.706 --> 00:02:24.688
There are tears on his golden face.

00:02:24.748 --> 00:02:27.860
His face is very beautiful.

00:02:27.920 --> 00:02:30.661
The little swallow is sad.

00:02:30.721 --> 00:02:32.202
Who are you?

00:02:32.261 --> 00:02:33.662
He asks.

00:02:33.722 --> 00:02:36.003
I am the happy prince.

00:02:36.063 --> 00:02:38.114
Why are you crying?"

00:02:38.174 --> 00:02:39.984
asks the swallow.

00:02:40.044 --> 00:02:43.696
The people in the city call me the Happy Prince.

00:02:43.755 --> 00:02:46.627
In the castle, I was happy.

00:02:46.687 --> 00:02:49.298
Everything there was beautiful.

00:02:49.358 --> 00:02:55.740
But now I am on this high column, and I can see all the misery of my city.

00:02:55.800 --> 00:02:59.682
My heart is made of metal, but I cry.

00:02:59.742 --> 00:03:03.763
Look, over there, there is a poor house.

00:03:03.823 --> 00:03:06.215
One of the windows is open.

00:03:06.274 --> 00:03:08.286
I can see a woman.

00:03:08.346 --> 00:03:10.616
She is very poor.

00:03:10.676 --> 00:03:12.957
There is a boy in bed.

00:03:13.017 --> 00:03:14.788
He is not well.

00:03:14.848 --> 00:03:17.309
He wants some oranges.

00:03:17.369 --> 00:03:21.100
His mother has nothing to give him except water.

00:03:21.160 --> 00:03:22.951
He is crying.

00:03:23.011 --> 00:03:28.543
Swallow, little swallow, can you take her the ruby from my sword?

00:03:28.603 --> 00:03:32.044
I must go to Egypt, says the swallow.

00:03:32.104 --> 00:03:33.814
My friends are there.

00:03:33.874 --> 00:03:37.144
They fly up and down the Nile River.

00:03:37.204 --> 00:03:39.556
They talk to the flowers.

00:03:39.616 --> 00:03:42.968
They sleep in the tomb of the Great King.

00:03:43.028 --> 00:03:46.330
Swallow, swallow, little swallow.

00:03:46.390 --> 00:03:47.811
Says the prince.

00:03:47.870 --> 00:03:52.163
Can you stay with me for one night and be my messenger?

00:03:52.223 --> 00:03:56.936
The boy is very ill and his mother is very sad.

00:03:56.996 --> 00:04:00.238
The happy prince is sad.

00:04:00.298 --> 00:04:02.800
The little swallow is sorry.

00:04:02.860 --> 00:04:06.234
It is very cold here, he says.

00:04:06.294 --> 00:04:11.840
But I can stay with you for one night and be your messenger.

00:04:11.900 --> 00:04:15.983
Thank you, little swallow, says the prince.

00:04:16.043 --> 00:04:22.140
The little swallow takes out the red ruby from the prince's sword.

00:04:22.200 --> 00:04:25.282
Then he flies away with the ruby.

00:04:25.342 --> 00:04:28.620
He flies over the houses of the city.

00:04:28.679 --> 00:04:34.788
He passes by the church and sees statues of white angels.

00:04:34.847 --> 00:04:40.460
He passes by the palace and hears lovely music.

00:04:40.520 --> 00:04:45.504
He flies over the river and sees the ships.

00:04:45.564 --> 00:04:51.296
At last he comes to the poor house and looks inside.

00:04:51.356 --> 00:04:56.667
The sick boy is in bed and his mother is sleeping.

00:04:56.727 --> 00:05:01.268
The little swallow puts the ruby on the table.

00:05:01.328 --> 00:05:11.576
Then he flies back to the happy prince and says, The night is cold, but I am warm now.

00:05:11.636 --> 00:05:14.810
Birds.

00:05:14.870 --> 00:05:19.914
There are about 9,000 types of birds in the world.

00:05:19.974 --> 00:05:22.830
All birds have feathers.

00:05:22.890 --> 00:05:28.369
Most birds have wings, but some birds can't fly.

00:05:28.428 --> 00:05:32.892
Let's look at some very interesting birds.

00:05:32.952 --> 00:05:38.036
Humming birds are the smallest birds in the world.

00:05:38.096 --> 00:05:41.880
They are about five centimetres long.

00:05:41.940 --> 00:05:49.375
Humming birds can fly slowly or quickly, up, down or backwards.

00:05:49.435 --> 00:05:53.386
Eagles are big, strong birds.

00:05:53.446 --> 00:05:56.755
Many eagles live in the mountains.

00:05:56.815 --> 00:05:59.915
They fly high in the sky.

00:05:59.975 --> 00:06:03.776
Penguins are birds, but they can't fly.

00:06:03.836 --> 00:06:05.566
They swim.

00:06:05.626 --> 00:06:09.268
Penguins live in Antarctica.

00:06:09.328 --> 00:06:13.689
The ostrich is the biggest bird in the world.

00:06:13.748 --> 00:06:17.589
It is about 2.4 metres tall.

00:06:17.649 --> 00:06:20.609
It lives in central Africa.

00:06:20.669 --> 00:06:26.322
It can't fly, but it runs very fast.

00:06:26.382 --> 00:06:29.334
Part 2.

00:06:29.394 --> 00:06:37.540
The Sapphire The next day, the little swallow has a bath in the river.

00:06:37.600 --> 00:06:41.083
There is a professor walking over the bridge.

00:06:41.142 --> 00:06:43.624
What a strange thing.

00:06:43.644 --> 00:06:46.348
A swallow in winter.

00:06:46.408 --> 00:06:48.041
says the professor.

00:06:48.101 --> 00:06:52.304
Tonight, I go to Egypt, says the swallow.

00:06:52.364 --> 00:06:56.606
So he visits the public monuments of the city.

00:06:56.666 --> 00:07:05.701
When the other winter birds see him, they are surprised and say, What a beautiful bird!

00:07:05.760 --> 00:07:10.477
This makes the little swallow very happy.

00:07:10.536 --> 00:07:18.246
In the evening, the swallow looks at the happy prince and says, I am going to Egypt.

00:07:18.306 --> 00:07:21.639
Swallow, swallow, little swallow.

00:07:21.699 --> 00:07:23.050
Says the prince.

00:07:23.110 --> 00:07:25.833
Can you stay with me another night?

00:07:25.892 --> 00:07:29.166
My friends are waiting for me in Egypt.

00:07:29.226 --> 00:07:32.809
Tomorrow, they are flying up the river.

00:07:32.868 --> 00:07:36.782
They are visiting the statue of the god Mamnon.

00:07:36.842 --> 00:07:42.032
At midday, The yellow lions go to the water and drink.

00:07:42.092 --> 00:07:48.358
They have big green eyes and a terrible roar.

00:07:48.418 --> 00:07:52.272
Swallow, swallow, little swallow.

00:07:52.332 --> 00:07:53.692
Says the prince.

00:07:53.752 --> 00:07:56.606
I can see a young man in an attic.

00:07:56.666 --> 00:07:58.227
He is a writer.

00:07:58.287 --> 00:08:02.038
He can't write because he is too cold and hungry.

00:08:02.098 --> 00:08:06.240
Well, I can stay with you another night.

00:08:06.300 --> 00:08:07.861
Says the swallow.

00:08:07.921 --> 00:08:10.533
Must I take him another Ruby?

00:08:10.593 --> 00:08:12.424
I haven't got a Ruby.

00:08:12.484 --> 00:08:13.766
Says the prince.

00:08:13.826 --> 00:08:15.927
I only have my eyes.

00:08:15.987 --> 00:08:18.639
They are made of blue sapphires.

00:08:18.699 --> 00:08:21.391
Take one of the sapphires to him.

00:08:21.451 --> 00:08:24.594
He can sell it and buy food and firewood.

00:08:24.653 --> 00:08:27.396
Then he can finish his book.

00:08:27.456 --> 00:08:29.027
Dear prince.

00:08:29.087 --> 00:08:30.438
Says the swallow.

00:08:30.498 --> 00:08:32.462
I can't do that.

00:08:32.521 --> 00:08:35.795
The swallow begins to cry.

00:08:35.856 --> 00:08:39.367
Swallow, swallow, little swallow.

00:08:39.427 --> 00:08:40.557
Says the prince.

00:08:40.617 --> 00:08:42.758
Do as I say.

00:08:42.818 --> 00:08:49.781
So the swallow takes out the prince's eye and flies to the writer's attic.

00:08:49.841 --> 00:08:55.003
When the writer sees the sapphire on his desk, he is very happy.

00:08:55.063 --> 00:08:57.414
Now I can finish my book.

00:08:57.474 --> 00:08:59.616
Says the young man.

00:08:59.676 --> 00:09:04.349
The next day, the little swallow flies to the port.

00:09:04.409 --> 00:09:07.140
He looks at all the ships.

00:09:07.200 --> 00:09:10.972
In the evening, he returns to the happy prince.

00:09:11.032 --> 00:09:13.653
I am here to say goodbye.

00:09:13.713 --> 00:09:17.695
He says, I am going to Egypt.

00:09:17.755 --> 00:09:21.076
Swallow, swallow, little swallow.

00:09:21.136 --> 00:09:22.527
Says the prince.

00:09:22.587 --> 00:09:25.438
Can you stay with me another night?

00:09:25.498 --> 00:09:29.248
It is winter, and it is cold here.

00:09:29.308 --> 00:09:32.836
In Egypt, the sun is warm.

00:09:32.896 --> 00:09:35.917
My friends are making a nest.

00:09:35.977 --> 00:09:39.658
Dear prince, I must leave you.

00:09:39.718 --> 00:09:44.249
Next spring, I can bring you a ruby and a sapphire."

00:09:44.309 --> 00:09:47.870
In the street below says the happy prince.

00:09:47.930 --> 00:09:50.091
There is a little match girl.

00:09:50.151 --> 00:09:54.492
Look, her matches are falling in a puddle of water.

00:09:54.552 --> 00:09:56.849
Now she can't sell them.

00:09:56.909 --> 00:09:58.826
She is crying.

00:09:58.886 --> 00:10:03.997
She is poor, and has no shoes.

00:10:04.057 --> 00:10:07.858
Take my other eye and give it to her.

00:10:07.918 --> 00:10:10.948
I can stay with you another night.

00:10:11.008 --> 00:10:12.479
Says the swallow.

00:10:12.539 --> 00:10:18.390
But I can't take out your other eye, because then you can't see.

00:10:18.450 --> 00:10:21.461
Swallow, swallow, little swallow.

00:10:21.521 --> 00:10:22.602
Says the prince.

00:10:22.662 --> 00:10:24.802
Do as I say.

00:10:24.862 --> 00:10:29.604
So the swallow takes out the prince's other eye.

00:10:29.664 --> 00:10:35.748
He flies to the little match girl and puts the sapphire in her hand.

00:10:35.808 --> 00:10:39.171
What a lovely piece of glass!

00:10:39.231 --> 00:10:41.422
Says the little girl.

00:10:41.482 --> 00:10:44.625
She laughs and runs home.

00:10:44.685 --> 00:10:47.908
The swallow returns to the prince.

00:10:47.968 --> 00:10:51.000
You can't see now.

00:10:51.060 --> 00:10:54.638
I want to stay with you always.

00:10:54.698 --> 00:10:56.505
No, little swallow.

00:10:56.565 --> 00:10:58.236
Says the poor prince.

00:10:58.296 --> 00:11:00.606
You must go to Egypt.

00:11:00.666 --> 00:11:04.608
I want to stay with you always.

00:11:04.668 --> 00:11:07.430
Says the swallow.

00:11:07.490 --> 00:11:10.201
Part 3.

00:11:10.261 --> 00:11:20.116
The Broken Heart The next day, the swallow tells the prince stories about strange places.

00:11:20.176 --> 00:11:25.078
In Egypt, There are red birds called ibises.

00:11:25.138 --> 00:11:29.052
They stand by the river Nile and catch fish.

00:11:29.112 --> 00:11:31.925
There is a sphinx too.

00:11:31.984 --> 00:11:35.858
It is very old and lives in the desert.

00:11:35.918 --> 00:11:38.610
It knows everything.

00:11:38.670 --> 00:11:41.862
There is a big green snake.

00:11:41.922 --> 00:11:44.874
It sleeps in a palm tree.

00:11:44.934 --> 00:11:48.418
Dear little swallow, says the prince.

00:11:48.478 --> 00:11:51.398
You tell me about marvellous things.

00:11:51.458 --> 00:11:54.807
But misery is the biggest mystery.

00:11:54.867 --> 00:11:59.630
Fly over the city and tell me what you see.

00:11:59.690 --> 00:12:04.123
So the little swallow flies over the city.

00:12:04.182 --> 00:12:08.595
He sees rich people in beautiful houses.

00:12:08.655 --> 00:12:13.148
He sees poor people in dark streets.

00:12:13.208 --> 00:12:18.171
He sees hungry children with white faces.

00:12:18.230 --> 00:12:20.993
They are very cold.

00:12:21.053 --> 00:12:26.466
He flies back to the prince and tells him everything.

00:12:26.526 --> 00:12:29.017
I am covered with gold.

00:12:29.077 --> 00:12:30.257
Says the prince.

00:12:30.317 --> 00:12:31.938
You must take it off.

00:12:31.998 --> 00:12:34.779
Then we can give the gold to the poor.

00:12:34.839 --> 00:12:39.771
The swallow takes off the gold, leaf by leaf.

00:12:39.831 --> 00:12:42.532
He takes it to the poor.

00:12:42.592 --> 00:12:46.494
Now the prince looks dull and grey.

00:12:46.554 --> 00:12:49.677
The children's faces are happy.

00:12:49.737 --> 00:12:52.892
They laugh and play in the streets.

00:12:52.952 --> 00:12:55.834
We've got bread now!

00:12:55.894 --> 00:13:03.330
They say, it is winter and it is very cold.

00:13:03.390 --> 00:13:07.884
There are some little boys skating on the ice.

00:13:07.944 --> 00:13:11.646
They are wearing red caps.

00:13:11.706 --> 00:13:16.590
The poor little swallow is very cold.

00:13:16.650 --> 00:13:23.072
He does not want to leave the prince He loves him very much.

00:13:23.132 --> 00:13:26.763
Goodbye, dear Prince.

00:13:26.823 --> 00:13:29.634
I am dying.

00:13:29.694 --> 00:13:33.056
Says the poor little swallow.

00:13:33.116 --> 00:13:39.458
He kisses the happy prince and dies near his feet.

00:13:39.518 --> 00:13:45.992
At that moment, there is a strange noise inside the statue.

00:13:46.052 --> 00:13:51.336
The prince's metal heart is breaking.

00:13:51.396 --> 00:13:56.250
It is certainly very cold.

00:13:56.310 --> 00:14:01.932
The next morning, the mayor of the city looks at the statue.

00:14:01.992 --> 00:14:06.673
Dear me, the prince looks very ugly.

00:14:06.733 --> 00:14:08.333
Yes.

00:14:08.353 --> 00:14:10.594
He looks very bad.

00:14:10.654 --> 00:14:13.125
Say the mayor's friends.

00:14:13.185 --> 00:14:16.446
They always agree with the mayor.

00:14:16.506 --> 00:14:20.218
There is a dead bird near his feet.

00:14:20.278 --> 00:14:23.802
Birds must not die here.

00:14:23.862 --> 00:14:28.733
So they pull down the statue of the happy prince.

00:14:28.793 --> 00:14:32.144
They melt the statue in a furnace.

00:14:32.204 --> 00:14:35.536
But the broken heart does not melt.

00:14:35.596 --> 00:14:37.266
How strange.

00:14:37.326 --> 00:14:38.577
Says a worker.

00:14:38.637 --> 00:14:42.388
The broken heart does not melt in the furnace.

00:14:42.448 --> 00:14:45.366
We must throw it away.

00:14:45.426 --> 00:14:51.876
The worker takes the broken heart and puts it near the dead swallow.

00:14:51.936 --> 00:14:56.728
Bring me the two most precious things in the city.

00:14:56.788 --> 00:15:00.700
Says God to his angel.

00:15:00.760 --> 00:15:06.964
The angel brings him the broken heart and the dead bird.

00:15:07.024 --> 00:15:08.854
Very well.

00:15:08.914 --> 00:15:10.354
Says God.

00:15:10.414 --> 00:15:21.769
In my garden of paradise, this little bird can sing and the happy prince can live forever.

00:15:21.829 --> 00:15:26.212
Exercise 6.

00:15:26.272 --> 00:15:31.285
Listen and circle the word you hear.

00:15:31.345 --> 00:15:37.080
There is a golden statue called the Happy Prince.

00:15:37.140 --> 00:15:42.532
A swallow stops near the statue to rest one night.

00:15:42.592 --> 00:15:47.354
He is going to Egypt because it is winter.

00:15:47.414 --> 00:15:54.007
The happy prince is crying because he can see the poor people in the city.

00:15:54.068 --> 00:15:58.789
The prince asks the swallow to help him.

00:15:58.849 --> 00:16:01.980
The swallow stays.

00:16:02.040 --> 00:16:07.024
He gives the poor people precious stones and gold.

00:16:07.084 --> 00:16:10.958
Now the prince is very dull.

00:16:11.018 --> 00:16:16.923
It's very cold, and the swallow dies.

00:16:16.983 --> 00:16:20.596
The prince's heart breaks.

00:16:20.656 --> 00:16:27.541
The next day, the mayor of the city orders to pull down the statue.

00:16:27.601 --> 00:16:33.505
An angel brings God the bird and the heart.

00:16:33.565 --> 00:16:41.736
God says the prince and the swallow can live in paradise forever.

00:16:41.796 --> 00:16:49.329
Migratory Birds There are many migratory birds in the world.

00:16:49.389 --> 00:16:54.360
Swallows, ducks and stalks are migratory birds.

00:16:54.420 --> 00:16:57.801
They build their nests in the north.

00:16:57.861 --> 00:17:02.806
Every autumn they fly long distances to the south.

00:17:02.866 --> 00:17:06.302
They fly together in big groups.

00:17:06.362 --> 00:17:10.973
In the south it is warmer and there is more food.

00:17:11.034 --> 00:17:16.196
Every spring they return to their nests in the north.

00:17:16.256 --> 00:17:25.301
Every year Swallows leave San Juan Capistrano in California on the 23rd of October.

00:17:25.362 --> 00:17:28.533
They fly to South America.

00:17:28.593 --> 00:17:32.799
They always return on the 19th of March.

00:17:32.860 --> 00:17:39.438
In autumn, wild ducks leave Scandinavia and Siberia.

00:17:39.498 --> 00:17:42.380
They fly to Central Europe.

00:17:42.440 --> 00:17:45.733
They return home in the spring.

00:17:45.794 --> 00:17:49.746
In autumn, stalks leave Western Europe.

00:17:49.806 --> 00:17:52.508
They fly to Central Africa.

00:17:52.568 --> 00:17:56.480
They return home in the spring, too.

00:17:56.540 --> 00:18:10.728
The Selfish Giant Part 1 Winter Every afternoon, the children play in the giant garden.

00:18:10.788 --> 00:18:16.751
It is a big, lovely garden with green grass.

00:18:16.812 --> 00:18:20.454
Beautiful flowers grow there.

00:18:20.514 --> 00:18:27.418
There are twelve peach trees with delicate pink blossoms.

00:18:27.478 --> 00:18:33.842
The birds sit on the trees and sing sweet songs.

00:18:33.903 --> 00:18:37.644
The children listen to the birds.

00:18:37.704 --> 00:18:40.886
How happy we are here!

00:18:40.946 --> 00:18:43.728
The children say.

00:18:43.788 --> 00:18:46.889
The giant is away.

00:18:46.949 --> 00:18:51.741
He is visiting his friend, the ogre.

00:18:51.802 --> 00:18:57.824
After seven years, the giant returns home.

00:18:57.884 --> 00:19:03.602
When he arrives, he sees the children in his garden.

00:19:03.662 --> 00:19:08.810
They are playing.

00:19:08.870 --> 00:19:15.053
What are you doing here?

00:19:15.113 --> 00:19:18.554
He says in a loud voice.

00:19:18.614 --> 00:19:23.468
The children are very scared and run away.

00:19:23.528 --> 00:19:28.050
This is my garden, my garden.

00:19:28.110 --> 00:19:29.952
Says the giant.

00:19:30.012 --> 00:19:33.815
Only I can play here.

00:19:33.875 --> 00:19:39.640
So the giant builds a high wall around the garden.

00:19:39.701 --> 00:19:45.974
Then he puts up a sign.

00:19:46.034 --> 00:19:52.860
No one must enter.

00:19:52.920 --> 00:19:57.773
He is a very selfish giant.

00:19:57.833 --> 00:20:03.792
Now the poor children have no place to play.

00:20:03.853 --> 00:20:07.240
They can't play on the road.

00:20:07.300 --> 00:20:13.673
There are big stones on the road and the children don't like them.

00:20:13.734 --> 00:20:19.487
After school, the children walk near the high wall.

00:20:19.547 --> 00:20:25.250
They talk about the beautiful garden inside.

00:20:25.310 --> 00:20:33.706
It is spring and there are little blossoms and little birds everywhere.

00:20:33.766 --> 00:20:41.078
But in the garden of the selfish giant, it is still winter.

00:20:41.138 --> 00:20:46.879
The birds do not sing there because there are no children.

00:20:46.939 --> 00:20:51.170
There are no blossoms on the trees.

00:20:51.230 --> 00:20:57.131
A beautiful flower puts its head out of the grass.

00:20:57.191 --> 00:21:00.162
It looks for the children.

00:21:00.222 --> 00:21:06.122
It sees the sign and goes back into the ground.

00:21:06.183 --> 00:21:09.715
It goes to sleep.

00:21:09.775 --> 00:21:15.478
Only the snow and the frost are happy.

00:21:15.538 --> 00:21:20.742
Spring doesn't come to this garden.

00:21:20.802 --> 00:21:27.883
They say, we can live here all year.

00:21:27.943 --> 00:21:35.372
The snow covers the grass with her big white cloak.

00:21:35.432 --> 00:21:40.272
The frost paints the trees silver.

00:21:40.332 --> 00:21:46.864
The snow and the frost invite the North Wind to stay with them.

00:21:46.924 --> 00:21:52.976
The North Wind comes and blows all day in the garden.

00:21:53.036 --> 00:21:59.655
He has a big warm coat and a hat.

00:21:59.715 --> 00:22:05.106
This is a wonderful place.

00:22:05.166 --> 00:22:07.607
Says the North Wind.

00:22:07.667 --> 00:22:11.700
We must invite the Hail.

00:22:11.760 --> 00:22:15.042
So the Hail comes.

00:22:15.102 --> 00:22:18.214
He is dressed in grain.

00:22:18.274 --> 00:22:23.188
For three days he runs around the garden.

00:22:23.248 --> 00:22:26.600
Then he dances on the roof.

00:22:26.660 --> 00:22:30.412
There is a lot of Hail.

00:22:30.471 --> 00:22:34.933
Why doesn't the spring come?"

00:22:34.993 --> 00:22:38.234
asks the selfish giant.

00:22:38.294 --> 00:22:45.885
He sits at the window and looks at his cold white garden.

00:22:45.946 --> 00:22:52.247
The spring never comes and the summer never comes.

00:22:52.307 --> 00:23:02.654
The autumn gives fruit to all gardens But it doesn't give any fruit to the selfish giant's garden.

00:23:02.714 --> 00:23:05.577
He is too selfish.

00:23:05.636 --> 00:23:08.199
The autumn says.

00:23:08.259 --> 00:23:13.082
So it is always winter there.

00:23:13.142 --> 00:23:23.470
The north wind, the hail, the frost and the snow live in the selfish giant's garden.

00:23:23.530 --> 00:23:26.350
Part two.

00:23:26.410 --> 00:23:28.862
Spring.

00:23:28.922 --> 00:23:34.897
One morning, the giant hears some lovely music.

00:23:34.957 --> 00:23:40.822
It must be the king's musicians.

00:23:40.882 --> 00:23:46.026
Says the giant.

00:23:46.086 --> 00:23:51.331
A little bird is singing a lovely song.

00:23:51.391 --> 00:23:55.534
The hail stops dancing on the roof.

00:23:55.595 --> 00:23:59.028
The north wind stops blowing.

00:23:59.088 --> 00:24:03.562
There is a sweet perfume in the air.

00:24:03.622 --> 00:24:10.426
I think spring is here at last, says the giant.

00:24:10.486 --> 00:24:15.671
He goes to the window and looks outside.

00:24:15.731 --> 00:24:19.176
What does he see?

00:24:19.236 --> 00:24:23.942
He sees something wonderful.

00:24:24.002 --> 00:24:27.984
There is a little hole in the wall.

00:24:28.044 --> 00:24:31.826
Now the children can enter the garden.

00:24:31.886 --> 00:24:36.490
There is a little child on every tree.

00:24:36.550 --> 00:24:40.452
The trees have beautiful blossoms.

00:24:40.512 --> 00:24:44.436
They are very happy to have the children.

00:24:44.496 --> 00:24:49.930
The birds are flying in the sky and singing.

00:24:49.990 --> 00:24:53.425
The flowers are laughing.

00:24:53.485 --> 00:24:57.609
There is happiness in the garden.

00:24:57.669 --> 00:25:03.624
But it is still winter in one corner of the garden.

00:25:03.684 --> 00:25:08.378
In that corner, there is a little boy.

00:25:08.438 --> 00:25:14.064
He is very small and he can't climb the tree.

00:25:14.124 --> 00:25:18.920
He is walking around the tree and crying.

00:25:18.980 --> 00:25:22.094
The tree is covered with snow.

00:25:22.154 --> 00:25:25.086
The North wind is blowing.

00:25:25.146 --> 00:25:28.077
Climb up, little boy.

00:25:28.138 --> 00:25:30.199
Says the tree.

00:25:30.259 --> 00:25:34.052
But the boy is too small.

00:25:34.112 --> 00:25:40.675
When he sees the little boy, the giant's heart melts.

00:25:40.735 --> 00:25:43.717
I am very selfish.

00:25:43.777 --> 00:25:49.170
He says, now I know why the spring does not come here.

00:25:49.231 --> 00:25:52.934
I must put that little boy on the tree.

00:25:52.994 --> 00:25:56.166
Then I must knock down the wall.

00:25:56.226 --> 00:26:01.600
My garden must be the children's playground forever.

00:26:01.660 --> 00:26:08.086
The giant opens his door and goes out into the garden.

00:26:08.146 --> 00:26:12.880
When the children see the giant, they are afraid.

00:26:12.940 --> 00:26:16.444
They run away.

00:26:16.504 --> 00:26:21.852
The winter returns to the garden.

00:26:21.912 --> 00:26:25.984
The little boy does not run away.

00:26:26.044 --> 00:26:28.396
He is crying.

00:26:28.456 --> 00:26:36.413
The giant takes him in his big hand and puts him on a branch of the tree.

00:26:36.473 --> 00:26:40.626
Suddenly, there are blossoms on the tree.

00:26:40.686 --> 00:26:43.604
The birds come and sing.

00:26:43.664 --> 00:26:47.081
The little boy is very happy.

00:26:47.141 --> 00:26:50.172
He kisses the giant.

00:26:50.232 --> 00:26:55.534
When the children see this, they come back to the garden.

00:26:55.594 --> 00:26:58.505
The spring comes back too.

00:26:58.565 --> 00:27:02.226
It is your garden now, little children.

00:27:02.286 --> 00:27:04.127
Says the giant.

00:27:04.187 --> 00:27:12.288
He takes a big axe and knocks down the wall.

00:27:12.348 --> 00:27:17.057
Exercise four.

00:27:17.117 --> 00:27:23.028
Listen to part of the text again and fill in the missing words.

00:27:23.088 --> 00:27:27.209
I think spring is here at last.

00:27:27.269 --> 00:27:29.269
Says the giant.

00:27:29.329 --> 00:27:34.360
He goes to the window and looks outside.

00:27:34.420 --> 00:27:37.501
What does he see?

00:27:37.561 --> 00:27:41.532
He sees something wonderful.

00:27:41.592 --> 00:27:45.590
There is a little hole in the wall.

00:27:45.650 --> 00:27:49.598
Now the children can enter the garden.

00:27:49.658 --> 00:27:53.880
There is a little child on every tree.

00:27:53.940 --> 00:27:57.882
The trees have beautiful blossoms.

00:27:57.942 --> 00:28:01.754
They are very happy to have the children.

00:28:01.814 --> 00:28:06.645
The birds are flying in the sky and singing.

00:28:06.706 --> 00:28:09.796
The flowers are laughing.

00:28:09.856 --> 00:28:14.462
There is happiness in the garden.

00:28:14.522 --> 00:28:26.411
Part 3 White Blossoms At 12 o'clock, people go to the market.

00:28:26.471 --> 00:28:34.354
They see the giant playing with the children in the beautiful garden.

00:28:34.414 --> 00:28:38.986
The children play all day.

00:28:39.046 --> 00:28:43.740
In the evening, they say goodbye to the giant.

00:28:43.800 --> 00:28:46.534
Where is the little boy?

00:28:46.594 --> 00:28:48.764
asks the giant.

00:28:48.824 --> 00:28:51.484
We don't know.

00:28:51.544 --> 00:28:53.715
Answer the children.

00:28:53.775 --> 00:28:57.656
You must tell him to come tomorrow.

00:28:57.716 --> 00:29:00.066
Says the giant.

00:29:00.126 --> 00:29:03.557
We don't know where he lives.

00:29:03.617 --> 00:29:06.057
Say the children.

00:29:06.117 --> 00:29:16.580
The giant is very sad and says, He is my little friend, and I want to see him.

00:29:16.640 --> 00:29:22.994
Every afternoon, after school, the children play with a giant.

00:29:23.054 --> 00:29:26.996
The giant is very kind to the children.

00:29:27.057 --> 00:29:32.689
But he wants to see his first little friend.

00:29:32.749 --> 00:29:36.251
Where is he?

00:29:36.311 --> 00:29:39.097
He says to himself.

00:29:39.157 --> 00:29:44.583
Many years pass and the giant grows old.

00:29:44.643 --> 00:29:47.544
He can't play with the children.

00:29:47.604 --> 00:29:55.225
So he sits in an enormous armchair and watches the children play.

00:29:55.285 --> 00:30:08.872
He looks at his garden and says, I have many beautiful flowers, but the children are the most beautiful flowers of all.

00:30:08.932 --> 00:30:15.166
One winter morning the giant looks out of his window.

00:30:15.226 --> 00:30:18.568
He does not hate the winter now.

00:30:18.628 --> 00:30:24.980
He knows that the spring is sleeping and that the flowers are resting.

00:30:25.040 --> 00:30:29.781
Suddenly he sees something marvellous.

00:30:29.842 --> 00:30:32.762
He looks and looks.

00:30:32.822 --> 00:30:35.872
He is very surprised.

00:30:35.932 --> 00:30:43.196
In a corner of the garden, there is a tree with lovely white blossoms.

00:30:43.256 --> 00:30:49.440
Its branches are golden and there is silver fruit on them.

00:30:49.500 --> 00:30:53.962
Under this tree, there is a little boy.

00:30:54.022 --> 00:30:58.024
It is the giant's little friend.

00:30:58.084 --> 00:31:01.457
The giant runs to the garden.

00:31:01.517 --> 00:31:03.854
He is very happy.

00:31:03.914 --> 00:31:10.072
He runs across the green grass and goes to the child.

00:31:10.133 --> 00:31:15.796
When he is near the child, he becomes angry.

00:31:15.856 --> 00:31:21.240
He says, What are these wounds?

00:31:21.300 --> 00:31:27.584
There are the marks of two nails on the child's hands and feet.

00:31:27.644 --> 00:31:30.065
What are these wounds?

00:31:30.125 --> 00:31:31.686
Says the giant.

00:31:31.746 --> 00:31:34.918
These are the wounds of love.

00:31:34.978 --> 00:31:37.058
Says the child.

00:31:37.118 --> 00:31:39.730
Who are you?

00:31:39.790 --> 00:31:42.502
asks the giant.

00:31:42.562 --> 00:31:46.734
The giant has a strange sensation.

00:31:46.794 --> 00:31:51.188
He kneels in front of the little child.

00:31:51.248 --> 00:31:59.222
The child smiles at the giant and says, You let me play in your garden.

00:31:59.282 --> 00:32:03.837
Today, you can come with me to my garden.

00:32:03.897 --> 00:32:07.200
It is paradise.

00:32:07.260 --> 00:32:14.684
When the children come to the garden, they find the giant dead under a tree.

00:32:14.744 --> 00:32:19.946
He is covered with white blossoms.

00:32:20.006 --> 00:32:24.078
Gardens.

00:32:24.138 --> 00:32:28.730
A garden is a beautiful place.

00:32:28.790 --> 00:32:32.054
Children play in gardens.

00:32:32.114 --> 00:32:38.448
Trees, bushes, grass and flowers are part of a garden.

00:32:38.508 --> 00:32:46.034
Birds, butterflies, insects and other little animals live there.

00:32:46.094 --> 00:32:49.256
Some gardens are small.

00:32:49.316 --> 00:32:52.076
Others are big.

00:32:52.136 --> 00:32:58.771
Palaces and castles usually have enormous gardens.

00:32:58.831 --> 00:33:06.796
Italian villas and palaces have beautiful gardens with statues and fountains.

00:33:06.856 --> 00:33:13.538
The bobbly gardens in Florence, Italy are a splendid example.

00:33:13.598 --> 00:33:19.792
In France and in England there are many lovely gardens.

00:33:19.852 --> 00:33:35.852
The gardens of the castles of the Loire Valley in France and Hampton Court in England Most American and British people have a flower or vegetable garden.

00:33:35.913 --> 00:33:41.796
They often have parties or barbecues in their gardens.

00:33:41.856 --> 00:33:46.730
Have you got green fingers?

00:33:46.790 --> 00:33:50.473
Let's plant an avocado stone.

00:33:50.534 --> 00:33:54.406
Silen, you can have an avocado plant.

00:33:54.466 --> 00:33:57.304
It's very easy.

00:33:57.365 --> 00:34:03.944
Take an avocado stone and wash it.

00:34:04.004 --> 00:34:07.496
Put three toothpicks in the stone.

00:34:07.557 --> 00:34:12.980
Put half of it in a glass of water.

00:34:13.040 --> 00:34:18.442
Put it near a window inside your house.

00:34:18.502 --> 00:34:23.115
Change the water every week.

00:34:23.175 --> 00:34:30.532
When you see the first roots, put the stone in a pot of earth.

00:34:30.592 --> 00:34:32.244
6.

00:34:32.304 --> 00:34:35.808
Keep the pot inside your house.

00:34:35.868 --> 00:34:38.810
Remember to water it every week.

